'''Big Brother 24''' is the 24th season of the broadcasted edition of ''[[Big Brother U.S. (franchise)|Big Brother (U.S.)]]'' and the 28th season overall.

This season introduced a new cast and featured several notable events and twists that shaped the game's dynamics. These included the dissolution of early majority alliances like [[Old Skool]] and [[Po's Pack]], the formation and long-term control of [[The Leftovers]] alliance, and the introduction of the [[Dynamic Duos|Festie Bestie]] twist and split house [[Double Eviction|double eviction]]. The season also saw [[Michael Bruner]]'s impressive competition performance, discussions about implicit bias leading to [[Kyle Capener]]'s eviction, and [[Taylor Hale]]'s journey from facing mistreatment to ultimately winning the game. Notably, this season crowned the first African-American female [[Winners (US)|winner]], who also made history by simultaneously winning [[America's Favorite Houseguest]].

==Background== 
[[File:BB24 Logo.jpg|thumb|200px|Promotional Logo]]
The season was first officially announced by CBS after the airing of the ''[[Big Brother 23 (US)]]'' finale, where host [[Julie Chen-Moonves]] reminded viewers that ''[[Celebrity Big Brother 3 (US)]]'' was happening as well in the coming winter, after its initial announcement a few weeks earlier.<ref>https://twitter.com/CBS/status/1443411593799163907</ref>
