==Controversies==
===Mistreatment of Taylor Hale===
[[Taylor Hale]], the eventual [[Winners (US)|winner]] of the season, faced significant mistreatment from other houseguests early in the game. She was subjected to microaggressions, social isolation, and unfounded accusations. This led to widespread criticism from fans and former houseguests, who called out the behavior as racist and bullying.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/big-brother-24s-taylor-hale-details-house-mistreatment/|title=Big Brother 24's Taylor Hale Details House Mistreatment: 'I Was Resistant to Believing It Was Racism'|website=Us Weekly|date=September 26, 2022|access-date=October 2, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.etonline.com/big-brother-alums-call-out-cast-for-bullying-taylor-hale-187444|title='Big Brother' Alums Call Out Cast for 'Bullying' Taylor Hale|website=Entertainment Tonight|date=July 11, 2022|access-date=October 2, 2024}}</ref>

[[Daniel Durston]] and [[Nicole Layog]] in particular faced backlash for their treatment of Taylor, most notably after an incident during the third week where Daniel berated a confused Taylor, blaming her for [[Paloma Aguilar]]'s [[Walking|voluntary exit]] from the game while insinuating that she was trying to do the same to Nicole. This outburst was widely condemned by viewers and led to calls for their removal from the show.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.goldderby.com/article/2022/big-brother-24-daniel-yells-taylor/|title='Big Brother 24' fans rage after Daniel yells at Taylor: 'He needs to be removed from the house'|website=Gold Derby|date=July 27, 2022|access-date=October 2, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cheatsheet.com/entertainment/big-brother-24-fans-call-cbs-remove-houseguest-yelling-taylor.html/|title='Big Brother 24': Fans Call on CBS to Remove a Houseguest for Yelling at Taylor|website=Showbiz Cheat Sheet|date=July 27, 2022|access-date=October 2, 2024}}</ref>

===Kyle Capener's Racial Optics===
[[Kyle Capener]] was criticized for suggesting an alliance based on race, proposing to target non-white houseguests. This led to his eventual eviction and a house meeting where his comments were addressed. Kyle later apologized for his actions both in the house and after his eviction.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.etonline.com/big-brother-houseguests-confront-kyle-capener-over-racial-comments-189941|title='Big Brother' Houseguests Confront Kyle Capener Over Racial Comments|website=Entertainment Tonight|date=August 31, 2022|access-date=October 2, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/big-brother-24s-kyle-capener-apologizes-for-racially-motivated-comments/|title=Big Brother 24's Kyle Capener Apologizes for 'Racially Motivated' Comments: 'I Take Full Accountability'|website=Us Weekly|date=September 5, 2022|access-date=October 2, 2024}}</ref>

===Production Intervention===
CBS and the show's producers were criticized for their handling of these issues, with many viewers calling for more direct intervention. In response, CBS released a statement acknowledging the concerns and promising to address them, including providing additional support and training for houseguests. <ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.vulture.com/article/big-brother-24-controversy-cbs-response.html|title=CBS Responds to Big Brother Racism Controversy|website=Vulture|date=July 21, 2022|access-date=October 2, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cbs.com/shows/big_brother/news/1010181/cbs-and-the-producers-of-big-brother-issue-statement-regarding-season-24/|title=CBS And The Producers Of Big Brother Issue Statement Regarding Season 24|website=CBS|date=July 21, 2022|access-date=October 2, 2024}}</ref>

==Trivia==
*This is the only season to feature no opening credits.
**[[Taylor Hale]] later confirmed that a user on Reddit was correct with their guess that it was a network mandate that later got reversed the following season.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/BigBrother/s/uWV0ylK1vp</ref><ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/BigBrother/s/BWkFORQcFh</ref>
**[[Taylor Hale|Taylor]] later shared in a ''Big Brother'' ChatBCC group that CBS wanted to try it in order to add more show content to the episodes, and since they noticed that the intros often got skipped when episodes were watched on streaming services. She also shared that the houseguests did not even film any poses for potential opening credits.<ref>https://chatbcc.com/bigbrother/m/msg_pwy645zujaof/msg_s9ivoyqvqkuv</ref>
*This season marks the return of the live studio audience during the eviction shows following its absence in the prior two seasons due to the [[The Impact of COVID-19 on Big Brother|COVID-19 Pandemic]]. The season started without an audience, but it returned at the first eviction of the [[The Jury|jury]] phase, on Day 44.
*Excluding celebrity seasons, this is the first season to feature a tied vote since [[Big Brother 19 (US)]].
*This is the first season since [[Big Brother 16 (US)]] to have multiple houseguests be nominated at least six times.
*This is the first season to have two houseguests win four or more Power of Vetos in a single season.
**In this case, this was achieved by [[Michael Bruner]] and [[Brittany Hoopes]] who won 6 and 4 POV's respectively.
**However, two of their POV wins were shared between both of them because of the [[Dynamic Duos|Festie Bestie]] twist; in total, only 8 POV competitions were won by either of them.
*This is the second civilian season in a row to crown an [[Taylor Hale|African-American]] winner, following Big Brother 23 with [[Xavier Prather]],
**Coincidentally, both winners are from Michigan.
*Paloma is the fourth ''Big Brother (US)'' contestant in history to [[Walking|walk]] from the game.
**This is the first season since [[Big Brother 19 (US)]] where a contestant walks from the game.
*This is the first season to have an African-American male and female in the final 2.
*This is the first season in Big Brother US (since the introduction of the Power of Veto) where no female houseguests won both HOH and POV, either together or in separate weeks.
**[[Brittany Hoopes|Brittany]] only won 4 POV's but no HOH's, while [[Jasmine Davis|Jasmine]] and [[Taylor Hale|Taylor]] won 1 HOH and 2 HOH's respectively, but no POV's.
**It would be immediately followed by [[Big Brother 25 (US)|Big Brother 25]]
*This is the first season since [[Big Brother 12 (US)]] where only one [[Brittany Hoopes|woman]] won a POV competition.
*This is the third season to feature a [[showmance]] in the final 2, following [[Big Brother 7 (US)]] and [[Big Brother 21 (US)]] respectively.
**This is the first one in which the woman won.
*This is the first season since [[Big Brother 15 (US)]] where neither of the final two Houseguests had more than 5 competition wins.
*This is the second civilian season to end on a Sunday, following [[Big Brother 9 (US)]]. 
*This is the first season to have the finale voting and reunion be held in the backyard instead of the stage.
*This is the first season where every Houseguest was nominated by the final 9. In every other season, the last houseguest would get nominated at final 8 or later.
*This is the fifth season where all three of the Final 3 Houseguests won multiple HOH competitions following ''[[Big Brother 8 (US)]]'', ''[[Big Brother 17 (US)]], [[Big Brother 19 (US)]],'' and ''[[Big Brother 21 (US)]]'' respectively.
**This is the first one to have a woman win.
*This is the ninth season to have four Houseguests win multiple POV competitions, following [[Big Brother 9 (US)]], [[Big Brother 13 (US)]], [[Big Brother 14 (US)]], [[Big Brother 16 (US)]], [[Big Brother 17 (US)]], [[Big Brother 18 (US)]], [[Big Brother 20 (US)]], and [[Big Brother 23 (US)]].
**This was accomplished by [[Michael Bruner|Michael]], [[Brittany Hoopes|Brittany]], [[Kyle Capener|Kyle]], and [[Monte Taylor|Monte]].
*This is the second season to have African-American Houseguests win a combined total of 7 HOH's in a season, following [[Big Brother 23 (US)]].
**It is the second season to feature African-American houseguests winning a combined total of 10 competition wins, following [[Big Brother 23 (US)]].
*[[Marvin Achi]], who was originally cast on this season before being removed from sequester and replaced with [[Joseph Abdin|Joseph]], would go on to appear on ''[[Big Brother Titans 1]]''.

